WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.134
A plan becomes real when people can carry it out.

2
00:00:03.334 --> 00:00:15.142
For Cedar Crossing's eight-week pilot, a designated
coordinator maintains the schedule, staff receive a
brief walkthrough, and the manager allocates time for
checking the room and reviewing feedback.

3
00:00:15.342 --> 00:00:22.011
Before launch, the team decides what to measure:
successful use, unmet requests, barriers, and staff
workload.

4
00:00:22.211 --> 00:00:27.983
It records a starting picture, checks progress during
the pilot, and reviews the full result at the end.

5
00:00:28.183 --> 00:00:32.712
Suppose satisfaction improves but staff time becomes
unsustainable.

6
00:00:32.912 --> 00:00:35.350
That is not an uncomplicated success.

7
00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:40.645
The library may adjust the schedule, simplify a process,
or reconsider the option.

8
00:00:40.845 --> 00:00:43.750
Evaluation belongs in the original plan.

9
00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:50.319
It connects the service outcome to the resources
required, and turns a one-time decision into a learning
cycle.

